<Base title="What is This Web?">
  <header class="page-head">
    <p class="eyebrow">start here</p>
    <h1>What is This Web?</h1>
    <p class="lede">A guide to exploring AI skills, tools, and community resources on ai.swegrowth.id.</p>
  </header>
  <h2>Explore AI skills</h2>
  <p><a href="/skill">AI Skills</a> is the community’s collection of shared workflows, prompts, and configurations. Search by words, then narrow the results by item type or category. Select a category to browse its skills, or open any entry to read the full details.</p>
  <h2>Discover more</h2>
  <p><a href="/tools">AI Tools</a> brings together providers, coding agents, and AI development environments. Search or filter the list by group, and choose how to sort the results.</p>
  <p><a href="/news">AI News Digest</a> collects weekly AI news, with links to the original articles. <a href="/daily-terms">SWE Daily Term</a> introduces a software engineering term each day.</p>
  <p><a href="/wanted">Wanted List</a> highlights ideas the community would like to see built. Browse the requests, or share a skill that answers one.</p>
  <h2>Share a skill</h2>
  <p>Choose <a href="/submit">Post a Skill</a> to contribute a workflow, prompt, configuration, or useful link. Sign in to your account, give it a title and category, then add its content as text, Markdown, a link, or a file. Once submitted, your skill is added to the collection.</p>
  <h2>Your account</h2>
  <p><a href="/register">Create an account</a> to share skills. Sign in to post, visit your <a href="/profile">profile</a>, change your password, or log out. You can also explore the site without an account.</p>
  <p>Learn about the project on the <a href="/about">About page</a>. View the site code: <a href="https://github.com/swegrowthid/sweg-ai-lists">Frontend</a> · <a href="https://github.com/swegrowthid/sweg-ai-lists-backend">Backend</a>.</p>
</Base>
